{50}{95}{y:b}SKERRY POINT LIGHTHOUSE
{105}{180}- Marta. The lamp is out.|- The lamp is not out.
{190}{256}It is dark, Marta. That is what out means.
{266}{316}- It is resting.|- It is a lamp.
{326}{371}Everything rests. Even lamps.
{381}{444}<i>She did not look up from her tea.</i>
{454}{535}- Ivo, in eleven weeks|you have not once been right.
{545}{589}I was right about the gulls.
{599}{664}You said there were four. There were nine.
{674}{732}Four of them were the important ones.
{742}{833}- Go and look at the lamp.|- I am looking at it from here.
{843}{880}From here it looks fine.
{890}{920}It is off.
{930}{965}It looks fine and off.
{975}{1017}<i>A long, wet silence.</i>
{1027}{1083}If a ship comes now, what do we say?
{1093}{1137}We say the lamp was resting.
{1147}{1209}- They will write that down.|- Let them.
{1219}{1260}They wrote down the gulls.
{1270}{1320}They wrote down four gulls, Ivo.
{1330}{1360}Nine.
{1370}{1411}- Fine. Nine.|- Thank you.
{1421}{1503}<i>Marta climbs the stairs. Ninety-eight of them.</i>
{1513}{1543}Ninety-eight!
{1553}{1619}It is ninety-seven. You count the landing.
{1629}{1665}The landing is a stair.
{1675}{1714}The landing is a landing.
{1724}{1754}- Marta?|- What.
{1764}{1794}Is it on?
{1804}{1870}<i>A pause the length of a lighthouse.</i>
{1880}{1910}It is on.
{1920}{1967}- So it was resting.|- Do not.
{1977}{2027}It was resting and now it is up.
{2037}{2067}Ivo.
{2077}{2119}Like a person. Like a gull.
{2129}{2166}Ivo, come and hold this.
